HTTPS: Relies on one specific server/domain staying alive forever.

Pinning: Keeps a file saved on at least one computer (like Pinata's servers or your PC) so the network can find it.

IPFS: Isn't on the blockchain, and isn't a single website. Even if every pinning service dies, as long as you save a backup of the image on your hard drive, you can always revive the exact same ipfs:// link later